# 0112: off-by-default Q4_K row-base repack for wave64 (XEON_Q4K_REPACK=1)
#
# What. On a 64-lane (SIMD-width-64) Metal device, 2D Q4_K weights in a private, WEIGHTS-usage
# buffer are stored, on-card only, in a row-base "repacked" layout. The upload path permutes the
# incoming bytes; every consumer that reads the quantized bytes was given a twin kernel reading
# the repacked layout, or is routed off the Metal backend. The host-visible canonical bytes are
# reproduced exactly on readback; tensor bytes on disk, nb01/nb1 and ggml_nbytes are unchanged.
# No on-card copy is added. This generalises the 0111 Q6_K machinery over the type; it does not
# copy it.
#
# Why. Q4_K spreads d/dmin/scales/qs across a 144-byte block, so a wave reads four scattered
# pieces per block per row. Grouping each field once per row puts every 16-byte qs load on a
# natural 16 B boundary and keeps whole fields contiguous, shortening the memory pipeline for the
# decode (mul_mv n=1), n=2..8 (mul_mv_ext) and prefill (mul_mm) kernels. Most production models
# are Q4_K_M, mostly Q4_K bytes, so this is the larger decode win.
#
# On-card layout. Per row, nb = ne00/256 Q4_K blocks, row length nb*144 B:
#   canonical block-major:  for b in nb: [ d 2 B | dmin 2 B | scales 12 B | qs 128 B ]
#   repacked field-major:   [ qs: nb*128 ][ scales: nb*12 ][ d: nb*2 ][ dmin: nb*2 ]
# Total bytes and row stride are identical. Within a field the original order is preserved.
# Rows are independent. Field order follows the kernel's loads: the decode (value-2 shape) reads
# qs first and needs it 16 B aligned; scales are byte loads; d/dmin are half loads read last.
# Alignment of every vector load: 144 = 9*16, so every row start is 16 B aligned for ANY nb; the
# qs field (nb*128) and each block's 16 B qs window stay 16 B aligned. Eligibility therefore does
# NOT need ne00 % 2048 (that gate was a Q6_K-only artifact of the 210-byte block).
#
# Range rule (B3/B4/B5). ggml_metal_repack_permute works on whole rows with offsets RELATIVE to
# the span start (never absolute tensor offsets), so a partial range never overruns a scratch
# buffer. Every set/get on a repacked tensor is row-granular read-modify-write:
#   read  = read the whole rows covering [offset, offset+size), un-permute into a temp, copy out
#           the requested bytes (ggml_metal_repack_read_canon).
#   set   = read those rows, un-permute, overlay the new bytes, permute, write the rows back
#           (ggml_metal_repack_write_canon). Edges of a chunked upload read rows not yet written;
#           harmless because a later chunk overwrites them.
# The set_tensor offset argument (not the buffer offset) decides the mark and must be 0; the
# record stores the FULL ggml_nbytes(t) range and the row stride t->nb[1], so a later chunk at
# offset > 0 resolves to the tensor and is permuted at row granularity.
#
# Eligibility (all must hold; decided at the first write at offset 0, recorded per buffer):
#   XEON_Q4K_REPACK == "1" at device init, simd_width == 64 (decided once at init); else nothing
#   tensor type Q4_K; ne[2] == 1 && ne[3] == 1 (not MUL_MAT_ID expert tensors);
#   no ne00 gate (144*nb is 16 B aligned for any nb); buffer private (not shared/unified),
#   usage & GGML_BACKEND_BUFFER_USAGE_WEIGHTS; not a DMoE arena (see marker); set_tensor offset
#   == 0; per-tensor record keyed to the tensor offset in the buffer, so views that start on a
#   repacked row boundary (whole-row multiple of the recorded row stride) still resolve to the
#   tensor; any other view (non-whole-row) is rejected: ggml_metal_repack_is_rejected() ->
#   supports_op false.
#
# Type gate (Q6_K stays byte-for-byte identical). ggml_metal_repack_type_on(t) returns
# g_xq6k_repack for Q6_K and g_xq4k_repack for Q4_K; ggml_metal_repack_shape_ok(t) keeps the
# Q6_K ne00%2048 && nb01%16 gate and adds no gate for Q4_K. With only XEON_Q4K_REPACK set,
# g_xq6k_repack is false, so no Q6_K tensor is ever eligible, permuted or recorded; the Q6_K
# path is the 0111 path unchanged. How known: the type gate is the only added branch and the
# Q6_K permute branch is byte-identical to 0111; the CPU check replays a Q6_K-only set and
# asserts identical records with and without XEON_Q4K_REPACK (Q6K_RECORDS_IDENTICAL_OK).
#
# Consumer table (every consumer of Q4_K on-card bytes; canonical = untouched):
#   path                                                         file:line            handling
#   MUL_MAT w64 n=1 decode                                       ggml-metal-ops.cpp    twin kernel_mul_mv_q4_K_f32_rb_w64
#                                                                                       (value-2 shape: uint4 loads, 8 lanes/block;
#                                                                                       nr0=16 wide, _r4 twin nr0=4 for small m,
#                                                                                       matching the canonical V3=2 pick; used for
#                                                                                       every n=1 repacked dispatch regardless of
#                                                                                       XEON_MV_Q4K_V2/V3)
#   MUL_MAT w64 n=2..8 (mul_mv_ext)                              ggml-metal-ops.cpp    twin kernel_mul_mv_ext_q4_K_f32_rb_w64_r1_{2,3,4,5,8}
#                                                                                       int row; r0ptg=1; r1ptg/nsg unchanged.
#                                                                                       The ext gate bypasses the nc2 rows test for a
#                                                                                       repacked src0 (nc2 has no rb twin), so n=2
#                                                                                       reaches this twin instead of the canonical nc2
#                                                                                       kernel that would read the repacked bytes as blocks.
#   MUL_MAT prefill n>=threshold (mul_mm)                        ggml-metal-ops.cpp    twin kernel_mul_mm_q4_K_{f32,f16}_rb_w64
#                                                                                       same tiling/threadgroup/smem as the default w64 tile;
#                                                                                       only dequantize differs
#   fused QKV (QVK q4_K q + Q6_K v + q4_K k)                     ggml-metal-ops.cpp    kernel_mul_mv_qvk_q4_K_q6_K_q4_K_layout<QRB,VRB,KRB>
#                                                                                       8 static name literals (one per QRB/VRB/KRB
#                                                                                       combo, no block-local buffer); each part its
#                                                                                       own layout; Q6_K part independently 0111-repacked or not
#   fused QKV (QVK q2_K q + q4_K v + q2_K k)                     ggml-metal-ops.cpp    kernel_mul_mv_qvk_q2_K_q4_K_rb_q2_K_f32
#                                                                                       V (q4_K) branch twin; Q2_K never repacked
#   GET_ROWS                                                     ggml-metal-ops.cpp    twin kernel_get_rows_q4_K_rb
#   every other op reading a repacked tensor                     ggml-metal-device.m   supports_op false
#   MUL_MAT_ID (3D Q4_K experts)                                 (not eligible)        canonical; ne[2]/ne[3] != 1 rejects repack
#   DMoE arena (batched upload / memset / readback / cpy)        llama-xeon-dmoe.cpp   canonical via marker; never repacked
#   SET_ROWS / MOE / quantize / flash-attn / conv / etc.         ggml-metal-device.m   supports_op false when a src is repacked
#   cpy_tensor / blit / memcpy between tensors                   ggml-metal-device.m   host round trip through get/set at offset 0,
#                                                                                       whole nbytes; never byte-blit a repacked row
#   DMoE bank upload path (ggml_metal_dmoe_upload_* / bank)      ggml-metal-*.m        canonical; arena marked canonical
#
# Kernel names + selection hooks (line numbers refer to the file in this patch):
#   dequantize_q4_K_rb()                                        kernels/dequantize.h   row-base twin helper
#   kernel_mul_mv_q4_K_f32_rb_w64                               kernels/mul_mv_w64.metal  value-2 shape; nr0=16, _r4 nr0=4
#   kernel_mul_mv_ext_q4_K_f32_rb_w64_r1_{2,3,4,5,8}            kernels/mul_mv_w64.metal
#   kernel_mul_mm_q4_K_f32_rb_w64 / _f16_rb_w64                 kernels/mul_mm_w64.metal
#   kernel_mul_mv_q4_K_f32_rb                                   kernels/mul_mv.metal  (QVK Q/K branches; standalone);
#                                                                                       faithful port of kernel_mul_mv_q4_K_f32_impl,
#                                                                                       only the address computation reads repacked fields
#   qvk_q4_K_q6_K_q4_K_body<QRB,VRB,KRB> + 7 rb host wrappers    kernels/mul_mv.metal
#   kernel_mul_mv_qvk_q2_K_q4_K_rb_q2_K_f32                     kernels/mul_mv.metal
#   kernel_get_rows_q4_K_rb                                     kernels/quantize.metal
#   hook mul_mv:    ggml_metal_library_get_pipeline_mul_mv      ggml-metal-device.cpp  (runs before _r4/_r8 w64; needs n=1, 2D, w64)
#   hook mul_mv_ext:ggml_metal_library_get_pipeline_mul_mv_ext  ggml-metal-device.cpp  (runs before kquant_ext; r0ptg=1)
#   hook mul_mm:    ggml_metal_library_get_pipeline_mul_mm      ggml-metal-device.cpp  (use_mm_manual && !has_tensor w64; twin mirrors default tile)
#   hook get_rows:  ggml_metal_library_get_pipeline_get_rows_rb ggml-metal-device.cpp  (now takes tsrc0)
#   hook qvk:       ggml_metal_fuse_qvk                         ggml-metal-ops.cpp
#   dispatch ext r0ptg:                                         ggml-metal-ops.cpp
#   gate:           ggml_metal_repack_enabled / _is_tensor / _is_rejected (single predicate;
#                                                                                       _is_tensor already checks the type flag)
#   init:           XEON_Q4K_REPACK read once in ggml_metal_device_init; simd_width==64 only
#
# Arena marker. Same as 0111: ggml_backend_metal_mark_canonical sets repack_canonical = true and
# clears the repack records (the field was renamed q6k_canonical -> repack_canonical); called
# from llama-xeon-dmoe.cpp after the arena is marked WEIGHTS and before any arena write. The
# marker is type-agnostic, so a Q4_K arena is excluded exactly as a Q6_K one.
#
# Upload/readback paths touched (every path that moves tensor bytes):
#   ggml_metal_buffer_set_tensor            ggml-metal-device.m   row-granular RMW permute into on-card layout
#   ggml_metal_buffer_set_tensor_2d         ggml-metal-device.m   GGML_ABORT on a repacked tensor (B6)
#   ggml_metal_buffer_memset_tensor         ggml-metal-device.m   GGML_ABORT on a repacked tensor (B6)
#   ggml_metal_buffer_get_tensor            ggml-metal-device.m   row-granular inverse permute (arbitrary range)
#   ggml_metal_buffer_cpy_tensor            ggml-metal-device.m   host round trip get/set at 0, nbytes; exact
#   ggml_metal_set_tensor_async             ggml-metal-context.m  routed to synchronous RMW set
#   ggml_metal_get_tensor_async             ggml-metal-context.m  routed to synchronous RMW get
#   DMoE uploader + bank upload             ggml-metal-device.m / ggml-metal-context.m  canonical; marker prevents repack
#   RAWGET (test-only)                      ggml-metal-device.m   XEON_Q4K_REPACK_RAWGET=1 returns raw on-card bytes
#
# Reduction order changed. The repacked kernels keep the Q4_K algebra bit-identical per lane
# (same nibbles/scales/d, same 1/16 and 1/256 folding). The n=1 decode sums via the value-2
# v3ns tree (8 lanes/block, simd_sum); the QVK Q/K parts and the standalone rb twin are now a
# faithful port of the canonical kernel_mul_mv_q4_K_f32_impl (same lane/row/reduction tree, only
# the address computation differs), so their reduction order matches canonical. Last-bit
# differences are possible on the n=1 decode; eval-mode tolerance decides. Unset or wave32:
# unchanged.
#
# Decode gain is ~0 for Q4_K. The canonical block_q4_K already puts qs at +16 in a 144-byte
# (=9*16) block, so the 16-byte qs loads are 16-B aligned in BOTH layouts; the repack groups the
# fields but does not remove a cache miss the decode already avoided. The win, if any, is the
# prefill (mul_mm) and n=2..8 (ext) paths, not n=1 decode.
#
# Off by default; unset or any other value leaves the default path byte-for-byte unchanged. The
# hot path adds a single bool check (ggml_metal_repack_enabled()) when no tensor is repacked.
# Nothing on 0109/0110 kernels or selection is altered; no new switch affects wave32.
#
# CPU-only verification (no GPU program, no engine build, no test-backend-ops run):
#   .scratch/xeonllm-0-2/evidence/t07/q4k_repack_cpu_check.py
